  "modeling_notes": [
    "The current program requires the same 31-credit core for every student and exactly one intact 15-credit track. The lower- and upper-level portions are split only to expose the 45-credit graduation audit; cross-group constraints prohibit mixing track components.",
    "The 74 credits after the major contain Connected Learning and remaining applicable credit. Connected Learning publishes a 33-46-credit range affected by placement, transfer status, course choices, and overlap, so its gates are not gross-summed as an independent additive block.",
    "CSCI-400 is required in the major and may satisfy both the Connected Learning capstone and Writing Intensive gates. Full-Stack course ART-321 may satisfy Creative and Artistic Practices. MATH-110 may satisfy the quantitative foundation while also serving as the CSCI-110 prerequisite.",
    "A student entering with an approved transfer-oriented associate degree is exempt from all Connected Learning requirements except CL-100 or CL-150 and CL-400 or a major capstone. The catalog does not say whether that exemption waives ART-321's separate CL-200 corequisite.",
    "The categorical current program table is the requirement authority. Historical and prospective term sequences are deliberately absent from the requirement tree."
  ],
